==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hnot|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|hnutuz|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|knu-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|kneu-|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Faroese {{term|nøt|lang=fo}}, Norwegian {{term|nøtt|lang=no}}, {{term|nòt|lang=no}}, Danish {{term|nød|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|nöt|lagn=sv}}, English {{term|nut|lang=en}}, Dutch {{term|noot|lang=nl}}, German {{term|Nuss|lang=de}}, and also Latin {{term|nux|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
